mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Platform API\n\nA VIP task-and-commission platform. Users register with a phone number, a password, a required promo code and a secondary withdrawal password; the operator signs in with a single fixed admin account.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- `register`, `login` and `adminLogin` are callable by an anonymous caller: they are the entry points that create a session, so no prior sign-in is required. `changeSecondaryPassword` and `touchSession` require a signed-in session created by `register` or `login`.\n- `getMyAccount` and `touchSession` require a signed-in session created by `register`, `login` or `adminLogin`, but they do not trap: an unregistered caller receives `null`. `touchSession` also refreshes the caller's online timestamp. An admin caller receives the fixed admin account view (`id = 0`, `phone` = the admin username).
- `getDailyProgress`, `listRecords`, `getRecord`, `listCommissions`, `listMyWithdrawals`, `listMyMessages`, `startTask`, `sendMessage` and `requestWithdrawal` require a signed-in session created by `register` or `login`; an unregistered caller receives the trap `Sign in required`. An admin session is not a user account, so the read endpoints return an empty result for it and the mutating ones (`startTask`, `sendMessage`, `requestWithdrawal`) reject it with `Sign in required`.
- `getServiceStatus` and `listVipConfigs` are open reads: they need no session and return the current service window and the per-VIP-level quota/rate configuration.\n- Every admin method (`listAccounts`, `addMoney`, `removeMoney`, `grantCommission`, `setVipLevel`, `setVipConfig`, `assignTaskToUser`, `assignTaskToVip`, `listPendingWithdrawals`, `approveWithdrawal`, `rejectWithdrawal`, `listConversations`, `listConversationMessages`, `replyToUser`, `setRechargeRequest`, `creditRecharge`, `setPendingRefund`, `setAccountBlocked`, `setSecondaryPassword`, `clearConversation`) requires the fixed admin account. A non-admin caller receives the trap `Unauthorized: admin only`.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. A direct API caller must call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call; the first initializer receives the admin role and subsequent callers receive the user role.\n\n## Passwords\n\n- Every password on the platform — the registration password, the secondary withdrawal password, and the admin password — requires at least 8 characters. Shorter values are rejected.\n- The admin accounts panel is the only surface that displays password values. `AdminAccountRow` carries `password` and `secondaryPassword` as recoverable plaintext, and it is returned only to an admin caller. `AccountView` never carries a password, so non-admin users never see any password value.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- All monetary amounts are integers in FCFA (no decimals).\n- Timestamps are nanosecond `Int` values from `Time.now()`.\n- `UserId` is a `Nat`; VIP levels are `#vip0` through `#vip3`; record statuses are `#soumission`, `#termine`, `#frozen`; withdrawal statuses are `#pending`, `#approved`, `#rejected`; attachment kinds are `#image`, `#video`, `#file`.\n- Promo codes are unique per account and required at registration.\n- Chat attachments are stored through platform object storage; the message carries the blob reference plus its kind, original file name and byte size.\n\n## Recharge and the insufficient-balance gate\n\n- The admin sets the recharge amount requested from a user with `setRechargeRequest`, and credits it with `creditRecharge`, which increases the user's available balance (`Solde disponible`).\n- The admin sets the promised refund amount with `setPendingRefund`; it is reported as `Montant de remboursement en attente`.\n- `startTask` is blocked while the account has no available balance. The caller receives the trap `insuffisant balance, contact the service form to continue`. The gate stays active until the admin credits a recharge, after which tasks resume normally.\n- `getDailyProgress` reports `availableBalance`, `pendingRefund`, `requestedRecharge`, `insufficientBalance` and `blocked` so the Demarrage zone can render the gate without a second call. `commissionEarned` mirrors `pendingRefund`.\n\n## Account blocking\n\n- The admin blocks or unblocks an account with `setAccountBlocked`. A blocked account cannot start tasks or request withdrawals: `startTask` and `requestWithdrawal` trap with `Account is blocked`.\n\n## Service hours\n\n- The customer-service desk is closed daily from 18:00 to 08:00 and reopens at 08:00 (UTC). `getServiceStatus` reports `isOpen`, `opensAtHour` and `closesAtHour`.\n- The backend enforces the window: `sendMessage` traps with `Service is closed, it reopens at 08:00` while the desk is closed. The frontend also disables the composer and shows the reopening time.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- A withdrawal starts as `#pending` and becomes `#approved` or `#rejected` once the admin reviews it. Poll `listMyWithdrawals` to observe the change.\n- A task record starts as `#soumission` when the admin assigns it and becomes `#termine` when the user starts it.\n- `getDailyProgress` reports `canStartTask`; when the day's quota is reached the flag is false and `startTask` traps with `Daily tasks are complete for today`.\n- Chat history is newest-first; pass `beforeId` from the oldest loaded message to page further back. `listConversations` pages by `beforeUserId`.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `startTask`, `sendMessage`, `requestWithdrawal`, `register`, `login` and every admin mutation are not idempotent: retrying a successful call creates a second record or a second balance change. Confirm the effect with the matching read method before retrying.\n- `approveWithdrawal` and `rejectWithdrawal` trap with `Withdrawal request already reviewed` on a second call, so a retry after a timeout is safe to attempt.\n- `removeMoney` and `approveWithdrawal` trap with `Insufficient balance` rather than allowing a negative balance.\n- `clearConversation` deletes every message in a user's thread and cannot be undone.\n\n## Data intelligence (OQL)\n\nThe canister exposes the Caffeine Object Query Layer through `schema()` and `execute()`. Both are controller-only: a non-controller caller is rejected, so the Data Intelligence agent reads as the platform controller while end users never read these tables directly.\n\n- `account` (primary key `id`) — one row per registered account: `id`, `phone`, `promoCode`, `referredBy` (empty string when none), `vipLevel` (text `vip0`..`vip3`), `balance`, `creditScore`, `blocked`, `lastSeen`, `createdAt`. Password values and hashes are hidden.\n- `taskRecord` (primary key `id`) — one row per assigned task: `id`, `userId`, `merchant`, `productDescription`, `thumbnailUrl`, `totalValue`, `commission`, `status` (text `soumission`/`termine`/`frozen`), `createdAt`.\n- `withdrawal` (primary key `id`) — one row per withdrawal request: `id`, `userId`, `amount`, `status` (text `pending`/`approved`/`rejected`), `reviewedAt` (0 when not yet reviewed), `createdAt`.\n- `commission` (primary key `id`) — one row per commission credit: `id`, `userId`, `amount`, `source`, `createdAt`.\n- `serviceMessage` (primary key `id`) — one row per customer-service chat message: `id`, `userId`, `fromAdmin`, `body`, `attachmentKind` (empty string when none), `attachmentName`, `attachmentSize`, `createdAt`.\n- `vipConfig` (primary key `level`) — one row per VIP level: `level` (text `vip0`..`vip3`), `dailyTaskQuota`, `commissionRate`.\n- `dailyCounter` (primary key `key`) — one row per per-user per-day counter: `key` (the counter key), `count` (tasks completed that day).\n- `rechargeRequest` (primary key `userId`) — one row per user with an admin-set recharge amount: `userId`, `amount`.\n- `pendingRefund` (primary key `userId`) — one row per user with an admin-promised refund: `userId`, `amount`.\n\nVariant columns are rendered as their lowercase tag text so queries can filter on exact literals. Timestamps are nanosecond `Int` values.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- Registration traps on a short phone number, a password under 8 characters, a secondary password under 8 characters, an empty or unknown promo code, and a phone number already registered.\n- `requestWithdrawal` traps on an amount below the 2000 FCFA minimum, a zero amount, an incorrect secondary password, incomplete daily tasks, an amount above the balance, and a blocked account.\n- `sendMessage` and `replyToUser` trap on an empty body, and `sendMessage` traps while the service desk is closed.\n- `listMyMessages` and `listConversationMessages` treat `limit = 0` as unbounded (capped at 100 rows per call). `listRecords`, `listCommissions`, `listMyWithdrawals`, `listAccounts`, `listPendingWithdrawals` and `listConversations` apply the same cap.\n"
  };
};
